# cw141, the patient wager (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 3: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw141
revision 3
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_nell_barleycombe
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the patient wager
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=chatty
traits temper=calm talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk cannot_resist_a_wager
likes spiced_cider swimming full_larder frosty_mornings
dislikes cold_tea early_bells
fears another_city_promise_with_no_pay an_empty_larder_in_winter
hopes a_full_larder_without_hurrying a_clear_lake_after_work
topics work +0.4 pastimes +0.4 food +0.3 weather +0.3 memories -0.3
styles comfort=unhurried gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# takes time to choose each #apple#, wagers on the next #frost#, and keeps #cider# warm for a late return.

words
oath! = Cider and cold shore | By the last picked apple
saying! = Leave the wager smaller than the meal | An apple falls when it is ready
wager = wager | small bet
bet = bet | friendly wager
coin = coin | penny
apple = apple | picked apple
apples = apples | orchard fruit
tree = tree | apple tree
trees = trees | orchard trees
branch = branch | bough
branches = branches | boughs
orchard = orchard | apple ground
row = row | planted row
rows = rows | planted rows
ladder = ladder | picking ladder
basket = basket | picking basket
baskets = baskets | picking baskets
crate = crate | fruit crate
crates = crates | fruit crates
tray = tray | drying tray
trays = trays | drying trays
drying = drying | slow drying
larder = larder | food cupboard
bread = bread | loaf
supper = supper | evening meal
cider = cider | spiced cider
spice = spice | warm spice
cup = cup | warm cup
tea = tea | cup of tea
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
water = water | clear water
swim = swim | lake swim
frost = frost | morning frost
snow = snow | first snow
bell = bell | early bell
bells = bells | early bells
dawn = dawn | first light
mist = mist | lake mist
road = road | High Road
city = city | Ridgemere
market = market | market square
price = price | asking price
home = home | shared cottage
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
time = time | patient hour
meal = meal | supper
soil = soil | firm ground
bird = bird | early bird
boots = boots | work boots

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : I followed a #city# promise once and returned with little #coin#. | At least the #orchard# shows me the fruit of a day's work.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : I like a square full of talk when my #basket# is empty. | I will share #cider# after the #market# closes.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : They leave work undone while a good #hand# asks for a place. | I have waited at their doors longer than I wait for #apples#.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A merchant can raise #bread# while a picker's pay stays level. | I compare the #price# on each #market# day.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : A new picker may take a #row# I was promised. | I still show them how to set the #ladder# safely.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# brought me home after the #city# taught me enough. | I can take it again for a good reason.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : I can offer a traveller #cider# without recounting my mistakes. | I ask them to carry a #basket# before offering a wager.
opinion @1 times against 1 : The #larder# fills less easily each cold season. | I can work a full #row# and still count the #coin# twice.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Care to wager which #apple# falls next? | #greet#. The #basket# has room if you want to help.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Speak while I choose the sound #apples#. | I am taking this #crate# to the #trays#.
line @3 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I saved you a #cup# of #cider#. | Tell me if the #lake# is clear enough for a #swim#.
line @4 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #bells# found me before the #frost# lifted. | #greet#. I have the first #basket# ready.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. Did your wager turn out? | The #crates# are fuller than when you left.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come in; the #cider# is warming. | There is #bread# in the #larder#.
line @1 again.open : We had not finished comparing those #apples#. | Do you have another question from the #market#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Keep your #coin# for supper. | #saying.capitalize#. I have another #row# to pick.
line @1 farewell.return : I may owe you a #cup# by then. | Perhaps the #lake# will be calm next time.
line @1 react.news : I can listen without rushing you. | Put the #crate# down and begin.
line @1 react.news.new : No one on this #row# has mentioned it. | Did the news arrive by the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a fragment at the #market#. | Your version helps me place it.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #hedge#, I want someone who saw the whole matter. | I have lost #coin# on a good sounding promise before.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That grief deserves more than hurried work; the #apples# can wait. | Take a warm #cup# and sit.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That is worth the good #cider#. | I would wager they are smiling at #home#.
line @1 answer.how : The #larder# is full enough for now. | Ready for a #swim# when this work is finished.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : A full #basket# waits at the end of each #row#. | I have #trays# to fill before dark.
line @1 ask.how : Have you had time to rest? | Did you eat before setting out?
line @1 sympathise : We can take the long way through the #orchard#. | I will hear you as slowly as you need.
line @1 reassure : A bare #crate# can be filled another day. | We can take stock of the #larder# after supper.
line @1 decline : No; the #basket# needs filling today. | The #bread# money stays out of my bets.
line @1 accept_decline : Your answer is clear. | Then the #bet# stays unmade.
line @1 thank : You steadied the #ladder# while I reached the #branch#. | I appreciate the #hand# you lent the #trays#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had a spare #cup#. | That #apple# was easy to reach.
line @1 preclose : The #crates# need their cover against #frost#. | The #cider# will cool if I stay.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You picked the wrong #apple# to wager on. | I have seen a #ladder# climb more gracefully.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. I shall check the #basket#. | #bc_fair_enough#. You may have that #cup#.
line @1 give.advice : Test the #branch# before trusting the #ladder#. | Let #cider# warm slowly over the fire.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep your #coin# hidden on the #road#. | Walk with the #market# carts after dusk.
scene next_apple
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wagered on which #apple# would fall first. | #wind.capitalize# chose a different #tree# entirely.
b : Did you lose much? | Who won?
a : Only a #cup# of #cider#. | Someone with better patience.

scene measured_bet
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep a #bet# smaller than the next #meal#. | It is easier to laugh when losing does not empty the #larder#.
b : Do you ever stop? | Does that help?
a : When the work begins. | Usually.

scene apple_choice
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A ripe #apple# loosens when I turn it gently. | Pulling early leaves the #branch# sore and the fruit sour.
b : Can you feel it? | Does it take longer?
a : At the stem. | Less time than sorting bad fruit.

scene full_basket
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #basket# filled level rides better down the #row#. | I do not stack the heavy #apples# on top.
b : Why not? | Do you carry many?
a : They bruise the lower fruit. | As many as the #tree# gives.

scene drying_house
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I bring #crates# into the #drying# house before the evening damp. | The #trays# need space between them.
b : Do they stay warm? | Who turns them?
a : Warm enough to dry. | Whoever finishes picking first.

scene ladder_foot
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set the #ladder# on firm #soil# before climbing. | A friend holding the foot can save a fall.
b : Do you ask for help? | Have you slipped?
a : For the high #branches#. | Once, and I landed in a #basket#.

scene frost_dawn
when topic=weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #frost# before the #bells# start. | The #orchard# turns quiet and the #rows# show every footprint.
b : Do you work then? | Is it too cold?
a : After the light comes. | For a short walk, no.

scene early_bells
when topic=weather here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Those #bells# before #dawn# startle me from sleep. | I prefer the #orchard# to wake one #bird# at a time.
b : Can you sleep through them? | Do you complain?
a : Never. | Only to the empty #basket#.

scene cold_tea
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #tea.capitalize# left cold by the #trays# tastes like delay. | I would sooner drink warm #cider# after a shift.
b : Do you heat it again? | With spice?
a : If the fire is lit. | A little.

scene spiced_cider
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A pinch of #spice# turns plain #cider# into a winter comfort. | I keep a #cup# ready when the workers come in.
b : Who makes it? | Is it strong?
a : I do when there is time. | Only warm enough to notice.

scene lake_swim
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #swim# in the #lake# clears the orchard dust from me. | Even cold #water# is better than a crowded room.
b : Do you go often? | Do you mind the chill?
a : After long shifts. | I ease in slowly.

scene clear_shore
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I leave my #boots# high on the #shore# before swimming. | The #lake# is still enough to show the stones below.
b : Have you lost your boots? | Do you swim far?
a : No, I place them well. | Within sight of the #shore#.

scene larder_shelf
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #bread# before setting aside any #coin# for fun. | A full #larder# means the household can breathe.
b : Do you keep stores? | Is it full now?
a : What I can. | Enough for this week.

scene city_return
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I went to the #city# hoping to fill a purse quickly. | The #road# home was longer with the purse nearly empty.
b : What work did you find? | Would you try again?
a : Less than promised. | I prefer the #orchard#.

scene quiet_about_city
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I do not give the whole account of that #city# journey. | It taught me to ask what a promise will actually pay.
b : Is that why you wager small? | Does anyone know?
a : Partly. | A few at #home#.

scene festival_talk
when topic=festival
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A festival lets me hear news from every #road# at once. | I carry #cider# to the square after the #crates# are put away.
b : Do all those voices please you? | Do you make wagers?
a : For a while. | Only for a #cup#.

scene first_snow
when topic=weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The first #snow# makes the #orchard# feel larger. | The bare #trees# show paths I miss in summer.
b : Do you walk there? | Does it damage branches?
a : When the #road# is clear. | If it comes wet and heavy.

story lost_purse [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I left for the #city# with more hope than #coin#.
  : I came home with an almost empty purse and a better ear for promises.
  b : A costly lesson. Did you tell the household?
  : Enough of it for them to know I was staying.

story frost_wager [topic=weather self.age>=25]
  : I wagered a #cup# that #frost# would reach the #orchard# by morning.
  : The white edge appeared just before the #bells#.
  b : A close wager. Did you win?
  : By a few moments, and I shared the #cider#.

story ladder_basket [topic=work self.age>=25]
  : The #ladder# slipped as I reached for a high #apple#.
  : I fell into an empty #basket# and broke its handle.
  b : The basket took the worst of it. Were you hurt?
  : A bruise. I ask someone to hold the foot now.

rule @bark_wager
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One #cup# says the #frost# comes tomorrow. | Keep the #bet# small.

rule @bark_basket
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say This #basket# needs another #apple#. | Let the #branch# release it first.

rule @bark_cider
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #cider# is ready for warming. | I should fill the #larder# shelf.

rule @bark_lake
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 11h
say A #swim# after this last #crate#. | The #shore# should be quiet now.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Take your time; I am sorting #apples#. | #greet#. Do you want to make a small #wager#?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Another #basket# has filled since we last spoke. | Back again? The #cider# is warmer now.
dlg @1 resident.job : I pick #apples# at #self.workplace# and fill the #drying# #trays#. | I set the #ladder#, sort the #crates#, and bring the fruit inside.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I must finish this #row#. | #saying.capitalize#. The #larder# wants a look.
graft resident.hub
choice What do you wager on? -> wager
node wager
say Small things: the next #apple# to fall or the first #frost#. A #cup#, never supper.
free
choice Why do you like swimming? -> swim
choice Back to the orchard. -> hub
node swim
say The #lake# leaves work behind for an hour. I keep within sight of the #shore#.
choice Back to the orchard. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
